WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.100
MAYA ANGELOU ONCE SAID, "EACH
ONE OF US HAS LIVED THROUGH SOME

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.360
DEVASTATION, SOME LONELINESS,
SOME WEATHER SUPERSTORM

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.225
OR SPIRITUAL SUPERSTORM.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:16.490
WHEN WE LOOK AT EACH OTHER WE
MUST SAY, I UNDERSTAND.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.680
I UNDERSTAND HOW YOU
FEEL, BECAUSE I HAVE BEEN

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:22.140
THERE MYSELF.”

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:26.800
MY GREAT FRIEND, FILMMAKER, AND
PHILANTHROPIST, TYLER PERRY,

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.417
PERSONIFIES EMPATHY.

00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:33.852
TYLER KNOWS WHAT IT IS TO BE
HUNGRY, TO BE WITHOUT A HOME, 

00:00:33.852 --> 00:00:35.836
TO FEEL UNSAFE AND UNCERTAIN.

00:00:36.408 --> 00:00:38.230
SO WHEN HE BUYS GROCERIES FOR

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:42.800
1,000 OF HIS NEIGHBORS, SUPPORTS
A WOMEN'S SHELTER, OR QUIETLY

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.010
PAYS TUITION FOR A HARD-WORKING
STUDENT, TYLER IS COMING FROM A

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.856
PLACE OF SHARED EXPERIENCE.

00:00:49.856 --> 00:00:51.500
TYLER PAID FOR THE FUNERALS OF

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.734
THE BLACK MEN WHOSE NAMES WERE
ON THE PLACARDS AT MARCHES.

00:00:55.734 --> 00:01:00.040
IN ATLANTA, WHERE HIS FILM
STUDIOS EMPLOY THOUSANDS,

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:03.370
HE CREATED CAMP QUARANTINE,
MAKING IT POSSIBLE

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:06.794
TO SAFELY CONTINUE
MAKING A LIVING.

00:01:06.794 --> 00:01:09.119
EVERYONE IN TYLER'S CAMP
HAS BEEN GIVEN

00:01:09.119 --> 00:01:11.310
ACCESS TO THE VACCINE.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:14.222
AND THIS WAS JUST
IN THE PAST YEAR.

00:01:17.101 --> 00:01:18.920
&gt;&gt; THE MOST GENEROUS PERSON
THAT I KNEW GROWING UP

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:21.250
WAS CLEARLY MY MOTHER.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:24.060
SHE TAUGHT ME TO NEVER LOOK FOR
SOMEBODY ELSE TO BE THE HERO

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.170
AND NEVER SIT AROUND
WAITING FOR CHARIOTS

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:28.189
FIND A WAY.
FIND A WAY.

00:01:28.189 --> 00:01:30.240
SHE WOULD SAY, 
JUNIOR, YOU FIND A WAY.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:33.189
IN THAT FINDING A WAY, SHE WOULD
ALWAYS ENCOURAGE ME

00:01:33.189 --> 00:01:34.840
TO HELP SOMEONE ELSE.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.490
I REMEMBER GETTING OUT OF BED,

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:38.840
AND LITERALLY STEPPING ON
SOMEONE ON THE FLOOR.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.752
AND I GO IN THE KITCHEN AND I'M LIKE, 
"WHO ARE THESE PEOPLE?"

00:01:40.752 --> 00:01:41.911
AND SHE LIKE,
"SHH, THEY NEEDED A

00:01:41.911 --> 00:01:42.771
PLACE TO STAY."

00:01:42.771 --> 00:01:44.531
SHE DIDN'T HAVE MUCH,
BUT WHATEVER SHE HAD

00:01:44.531 --> 00:01:45.600
SHE WAS WILLING TO SHARE.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.160
SO, THAT'S VERY MUCH IN MY DNA.

00:01:48.909 --> 00:01:50.460
&gt;&gt; IT IS HOW HE WAS RAISED.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.439
THAT IF SOMEBODY REACHES
OUT, THEN YOU REACH OUT

00:01:53.439 --> 00:01:54.650
TO SOMEBODY ELSE, AND
THEN THEY'LL REACH

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:55.650
OUT TO SOMEBODY ELSE.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:58.680
&gt;&gt; WHEN COVID HIT, IT WAS 
REALLY IMPORTANT FOR ME TO

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.090
GET EVERYBODY BACK TO WORK.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:01.090
I'M ALWAYS THE PERSON

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:02.670
THAT SAYS OKAY, THIS IS
HAPPENING, WHAT DO

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:03.670
WE DO TO FIX IT?

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:05.180
HOW DO WE FIGHT IT?

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:09.259
&gt;&gt; HE FED ALL THESE PEOPLE
DURING THE PANDEMIC.

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:14.160
HE MADE SURE PEOPLE HAD WHAT
THEY NEEDED TO GET THROUGH IT.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.560
&gt;&gt; THE PERRY FOUNDATION
HAS BEEN ABOUT TRANSFERRING

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.700
TRAGEDY INTO TRIUMPH.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.080
I DON'T WANT TO HAVE A FOUNDATION

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:21.349
THAT IS TARGETED AT ONE
SPECIFIC THING, BECAUSE

00:02:21.349 --> 00:02:24.000
THE NEED IS SO GREAT
ALL OVER MANY THINGS.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.340
BATTERED WOMEN, TRAFFICKED
CHILDREN, POVERTY,

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.780
HOMELESSNESS, ADDICTION,
WHATEVER WE CAN DO,

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:30.570
WHEREVER WE CAN SHOW
UP TO HELP.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:33.720
&gt;&gt; THERE'S NO HARM IN CARING.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.890
HE'S GOING TO CREATE
OPPORTUNITIES FOR OTHER PEOPLE,

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:39.819
LIKE OPPORTUNITIES
WERE CREATED FOR HIM.

00:02:39.819 --> 00:02:41.250
HE'S GOING TO ENCOURAGE
OTHER PEOPLE,

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:45.230
THE WAY PEOPLE
ENCOURAGED HIM.

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:47.200
&gt;&gt; WHEN YOU'VE BEEN GIVEN A
VOICE, THERE'S A HUGE

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:51.590
RESPONSIBILITY TO USE IT IN A
WAY THAT SUSTAINS CHANGE.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:55.270
&gt;&gt; SO, HE CREATED A LIVING LEGACY
THAT KEEPS ON GIVING.

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:57.704
WHAT'S BETTER THAN THAT?

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:04.110
THIS MAN EXEMPLIFIES THE BEST
YOU COULD ASK FROM ANY HUMAN

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:10.010
AND THAT IS TO CARE ABOUT
YOUR FELLOW HUMAN BEINGS.

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:12.716
&gt;&gt; IT GOES BACK TO MY MOTHER,
JUNIOR, FIND A WAY.

00:03:12.716 --> 00:03:15.370
FIND A WAY.

00:03:18.053 --> 00:03:23.010
[ CHEERS AND APPLAUSE ]

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:28.930
&gt;&gt; TYLER, I KNOW YOU NEVER DO
WHAT YOU DO FOR THANKS, BUT I AM

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:30.909
GRATEFUL FOR THE COUNTLESS
WAYS YOU WORK TO

00:03:30.909 --> 00:03:33.260
MAKE OURS A BETTER WORLD.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:36.209
IT IS MY HONOR TO PRESENT TO YOU
THE JEAN HERSHOLT

00:03:36.209 --> 00:03:38.530
HUMANITARIAN AWARD.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:43.030
[ CHEERS AND APPLAUSE ]

00:03:57.082 --> 00:03:59.212
THANK YOU.

00:04:02.289 --> 00:04:07.065
THANK YOU,
THAT IS, THAT’S INCREDIBLY KIND.

00:04:07.075 --> 00:04:08.574
THANK YOU SO MUCH.

00:04:08.574 --> 00:04:09.621
THEY ONLY GAVE ME 
A FEW MINUTES, 

00:04:09.621 --> 00:04:11.930
SO I WANNA SAY A 
VERY SPECIAL THANKS

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:14.540
TO MISS VIOLA DAVIS,
WHO IS NOMINATED TONIGHT

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:15.988
AND DOING THIS.
THANK YOU, THANK YOU,

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:17.540
I REALLY APPRECIATE IT.

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:19.250
TO THE BOARD OF GOVERNORS,

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:22.340
ESPECIALLY TO WHOOPI
GOLDBERG, AVA.

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:24.500
YOU KNOW WHEN I SET OUT
TO HELP SOMEONE,

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:26.540
IT IS MY INTENTION TO
DO JUST THAT.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:28.720
I’M NOT TRYING TO DO ANYTHING
OTHER THAN MEET SOMEBODY

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:30.050
AT THEIR HUMANITY.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:32.251
LIKE, CASE IN POINT,
THIS ONE TIME I REMEMBER I WAS,

00:04:32.251 --> 00:04:34.060
MAYBE IT WAS ABOUT
17 YEARS AGO.

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:35.060
I RENTED THIS BUILDING 

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:37.190
AND WE WERE
USING IT FOR PRODUCTION

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:39.690
AND I WAS WALKING TO MY
CAR ONE DAY AND I SEE THIS

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:42.000
WOMAN COMING UP OUT
OF THE CORNER OF MY EYE

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.980
AND I SAY, SHE’S HOMELESS,
LET ME GIVE HER SOME MONEY.

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:45.526
JUDGMENT.

00:04:45.526 --> 00:04:46.990
I WISH I HAD TIME
TO TALK ABOUT JUDGMENT.

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:49.203
ANYWAY, I REACH IN MY POCKET
AND I’M ABOUT TO GIVE

00:04:49.203 --> 00:04:50.903
HER THE MONEY.
SHE SAYS, “EXCUSE ME SIR.

00:04:50.903 --> 00:04:52.540
DO YOU HAVE ANY SHOES?”

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:53.770
IT STOPPED ME COLD BECAUSE

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:57.080
I REMEMBER BEING HOMELESS
AND HAVING ONE PAIR OF SHOES

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:58.830
AND THEY WERE BENT OVER
AT THE HEELS.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:04:59.830
SO I WAS LIKE, YEAH.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:01.500
SO I TOOK HER INTO THE STUDIO.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.400
SHE WAS HESITANT TO GO IN,
BUT WE WENT IN.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.940
WE GO TO WARDROBE AND
THERE ARE ALL THESE BOXES AND

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:09.780
EVERYTHING AROUND THE WALLS
AND FABRICS AND RACKS OF CLOTHES.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:12.840
SO WE ENDED UP HAVING TO
STAND IN THE MIDDLE OF THE FLOOR.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:15.180
SO AS WE’RE STANDING THERE
IN WARDROBE, WE FIND HER SOME SHOES,

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:16.270
WE HELP HER PUT THEM ON.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:17.741
I STAND UP, I’M WAITING FOR HER

00:05:17.741 --> 00:05:20.270
TO LOOK UP AND ALL THIS TIME
SHE’S LOOKING DOWN.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:21.270
SHE FINALLY LOOKS UP.

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:22.610
SHE’S GOT TEARS IN HER EYES.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:26.850
SHE SAID, “THANK YOU, JESUS,
MY FEET ARE OFF THE GROUND.”

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:30.223
IN THAT MOMENT I JUST RECALL HER
SAYING TO ME, “I THOUGHT

00:05:30.223 --> 00:05:31.910
YOU WOULD HATE ME FOR ASKING.”

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:34.920
I’M LIKE HOW CAN I HATE YOU
WHEN I USED TO BE YOU?

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:36.310
HOW CAN I HATE YOU WHEN
I HAD A MOTHER WHO

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:40.380
GREW UP IN A JIM CROW SOUTH
IN LOUISIANA, RURAL LOUISIANA

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:42.080
RIGHT ACROSS THE BORDER
FROM MISSISSIPPI,

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:44.479
WHO AT 9 OR 10 YEARS OLD
WAS GRIEVING THE DEATH OF

00:05:44.479 --> 00:05:45.479
EMMETT TILL.

00:05:45.479 --> 00:05:46.990
AS SHE GOT
A LITTLE BIT OLDER.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.090
SHE WAS GRIEVING THE
DEATH OF THE CIVIL RIGHTS BOYS

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:52.350
AND THE LITTLE GIRLS WHO
WERE IN THE BOMBING IN ALABAMA.

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:55.060
SHE GRIEVED ALL THIS, ALL
THESE YEARS AND I REMEMBER

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:56.410
BEING A LITTLE BOY
AND COMING HOME,

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:57.850
AND SHE WAS AT HOME BEING LIKE
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HOME?

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:58.850
YOU'RE SUPPOSED TO 
BE AT WORK.

00:05:58.850 --> 00:05:59.850
SHE WAS IN TEARS THAT DAY.

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:01.919
SHE SAID THERE WAS A BOMB
THREAT AND SHE COULDN'T

00:06:01.919 --> 00:06:04.420
BELIEVE THAT SOMEONE WANTED
TO BLOW UP THIS PLACE

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:05.630
WHERE SHE WORKED.

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:06.970
WHERE SHE TOOK CARE 
OF ALL THESE TODDLERS.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:08.950
IT WAS THE JEWISH
COMMUNITY CENTER.

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:11.940
MY MOTHER TAUGHT ME TO
REFUSE HATE.

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:14.960
SHE TAUGHT ME TO REFUSE
BLANKET JUDGMENT,

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:17.660
AND IN THIS TIME, AND WITH
ALL OF THE INTERNET AND

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:20.210
SOCIAL MEDIA AND ALGORITHMS
AND EVERYTHING THAT WANTS

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:23.180
US TO THINK A CERTAIN WAY,
THE 24-HOUR NEWS CYCLE,

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:26.190
IT IS MY HOPE THAT ALL OF US
WOULD TEACH OUR KIDS

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:28.930
AND I WANT TO REMEMBER,
JUST REFUSE HATE.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:30.400
DON’T HATE ANYBODY.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:31.830
I REFUSE TO HATE SOMEONE

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:35.577
BECAUSE THEY ARE MEXICAN
OR BECAUSE THEY ARE BLACK

00:06:35.577 --> 00:06:39.274
OR WHITE OR LGBTQ.

00:06:39.274 --> 00:06:40.710
I REFUSE TO HATE SOMEONE

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:42.460
BECAUSE THEY ARE
A POLICE OFFICER.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:45.580
I REFUSE TO HATE SOMEONE
BECAUSE THEY ARE ASIAN.

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:48.660
I WOULD HOPE THAT WE WOULD
REFUSE HATE AND I WANT TO

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:51.580
TAKE THIS JEAN HERSHOLT
HUMANITARIAN AWARD

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:54.729
AND DEDICATE IT TO ANYONE
WHO WANTS TO STAND

00:06:54.729 --> 00:06:57.430
IN THE MIDDLE, NO MATTER
WHAT’S AROUND THE WALL.

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:59.270
STAND IN THE MIDDLE ’CAUSE
THAT’S WHERE HEALING HAPPENS.

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:00.830
THAT’S WHERE CONVERSATION
HAPPENS.

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:01.992
THAT’S WHERE CHANGE HAPPENS.

00:07:01.992 --> 00:07:03.722
IT HAPPENS IN
THE MIDDLE.

00:07:03.722 --> 00:07:04.222
SO ANYONE WHO

00:07:04.222 --> 00:07:07.020
WANTS TO MEET ME IN
THE MIDDLE, TO REFUSE HATE,

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:10.229
TO REFUSE BLANKET JUDGMENT,
AND TO HELP LIFT SOMEONE’S

00:07:10.229 --> 00:07:12.770
FEET OFF THE GROUND,
THIS ONE IS FOR YOU TOO.

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:14.512
GOD BLESS YOU AND
THANK YOU ACADEMY.

00:07:14.512 --> 00:07:15.512
I APPRECIATE IT.

00:07:15.512 --> 00:07:16.288
THANK YOU.

